    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94413.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Well, I worked closely with our superintendents who, by the way, we had going through the COVID pandemic just in the last season. It was very important that we opened up our national parks. You think about social distancing, boy, there's no better way to kind of help people get through a pandemic than to get them in the great outdoors. In fact, I saw a t-shirt the other day that said Montana, practicing social distancing since 1889. That was statehood. I mean, we're used to that in a place like Montana. And so I hope we will keep our national parks open. Yes, take the proper precautions in place where you might have more concentration of people, but it is much better to open our parks, not close and restrict them during a pandemic. One, for the physical health, but also mental health. The American people, we need to be outdoors more and the more you're outdoors, frankly, it helps the mind.",
