    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/4/94413.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 21,
    "turn_text": "Well, you're exactly right. The first point you made there, Gabriella, as it relates to, I think it's important to me to you to teach an understanding of the Second Amendment to future generations that James Madison and Thomas Jefferson were not in a room. They're concerned about the threat of white tales or amylope. And that's why we needed to be able to have firearms. Remember, the Second Amendment is not about hunting. It is about liberty. It is about freedom. And that's a very important foundational principle, understanding why we have the Second Amendment, which followed the first amendment, which is protecting critical rights on speech and religion and freedom of the press and petition and so forth. But to your point around the connection to hunting, and",
