    "turn_text": "is if you want to, first of all, preserve the great outdoors and preserve wildlife, you need to continue to encourage hunting because some of those dollars flow towards conservation and protection species. We see that in Africa. I've never been over in Africa to hunt, but you've If you actually hunt in Africa, they allow it. It actually reminds us to go out for the poachers. You actually protect a species when you hunt a species. It's counterintuitive to many who understand. the outdoors understand hunting. So that point around was laced to gun control. If you start shutting down on being able to procure firearms or ammunition, that will have an effect on conservation in a negative way, which again, might seem counterintuitive to those who understand really what hunting is all about in terms of actually protecting and promoting wildlife.",
